course: dictionary
lesson: 7420
title: A helper in uniform
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A policeman is a man who belongs to the police, the people whose job is to keep people safe and make sure laws are obeyed. Look at the words around the word for clues. «Two large country policemen are running after him!» Running after someone suggests they are chasing a person, so policemen are the ones who go after people.
explain: The word policeman has the word man inside it, so it names a man. Another sentence says «Toad may be brought back on a stretcher, or between two policemen», so policemen are the people who bring someone back. A good check is to swap in another word, such as helper. The sentence still works, but it loses the clue that these helpers belong to the police.
explain: In safety lessons you learn that a policeman is someone to go to if you are lost or in danger. In an emergency you call the emergency number: 999 in the UK and Ireland, 911 in the USA and Canada, 000 in Australia, or 111 in New Zealand.
fact: A policeman is a man who is a member of the police.
fact: Policemen keep people safe and make sure laws are obeyed.
fact: «A policeman's truncheon» means a policeman's short club.
fact: If you are lost or in danger, go to a policeman or call the emergency number.
fact: Emergency numbers: 999 in the UK and Ireland, 911 in the USA and Canada, 000 in Australia, 111 in New Zealand.
exercise: «Toad may be brought back between two policemen.» What is a policeman? | A driver who races cars | A sandwich in a case | *A man who is a member of the police | A tree that grows on the hill
exercise: «A policeman's truncheon» is a short club. Which word in this phrase tells you whose club it is? | club | truncheon | *policeman's | a
exercise: You are lost in a big town. Who should you go to for help? | *A policeman | A flask of tea | A pigeon on the path | A cutlass
test: In Australia, which number should you call in an emergency? | 911 | *000 | 111 | 999
test: What does a policeman do? | Grows apples in the orchard | *Keeps people safe and makes sure laws are obeyed | Sells tickets on trains | Bakes bread for the village
exam: Why should you go to a policeman if you are in danger? | Because policemen sell sandwiches | Because policemen grow crops on farms | *Because policemen keep people safe | Because policemen drive ships
